# Paths are relative to rootDir (src/), so only the manifest, the .gs files
# and the served .html are pushed. Anything else that ever lands in src/ is
# excluded by default rather than by being listed — safer as the project grows.
#
# The default-deny is the right shape and it has one failure mode, which the
# web app hit: a new *kind* of file is dropped in silence. `clasp push` lists
# what it sent and says nothing about what it skipped, so `page.html` stayed
# behind while the push reported success and the .gs half of the feature was
# live. `tests/manifest.test.mjs` now fails if anything under src/ is not
# pushable, which is the one thing a file test can prove here.
**/**
!appsscript.json
!*.gs
!*.html
